# arc-runner.user-md -- project rules for multi-step workers (Berreman)

This is the Berreman project prompt piece that pairs with the
cross-repo `arc-runner.system-md`. The arc-runner passes both
paths to each worker session; the worker reads this file *second*
(after the system prompt) for project-specific rules.

This file lives at `./.user-md/Berreman/arc-runner.user-md`
(repo-root relative).

**Usage (arc-runner-driven, never user-typed):**

```
Do the task <slice-spec-path> using
<this-tool-repo>/src/ai_strategy_generator/multistep/arc-runner.system-md
and ./.user-md/Berreman/arc-runner.user-md.
```

**Example:**

```
Do the task ./specs/001-01-scratch-one.md using
<this-tool-repo>/src/ai_strategy_generator/multistep/arc-runner.system-md
and ./.user-md/Berreman/arc-runner.user-md.
```

`<this-tool-repo>` resolves to the AI-Strategy-Generator clone
location on the host machine.

---

## Project shape

**Canonical source:** `./AGENTS.md` (repo root; `CLAUDE.md` only
imports it). Read it in full before the first edit: it is the
restart point, the style guide and the rule book.

In short, one solution, `Berreman/Berreman.slnx` (x64 only), holds two things:

- **the solver**: `Berreman/Berreman/` (Core), `Berreman/OpticalModel/`,
  `Berreman/OpticalProperties/` and `Berreman/Analytics/`, shipped as
  NuGet packages, over the vendored `MathNetNumerics/` projects;
- **Optical Constructor**: `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/` (Domain,
  Optimization, Storage, Seeding, Database, Controls, Ui, App, and the
  TestWindows diagnostic heads), an Avalonia FuncUI desktop app.

The test projects are `Berreman/BerremanTests/`,
`OpticalConstructor.Tests/` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/`
(Avalonia.Headless). There is no Android, no device and no emulator.
`BerremanRunner/` and `BerremanModelGenerator/` are stale and are not
in the solution.

---

## Build tool

```
dotnet build Berreman.slnx -c Release
```

Run it from the `Berreman/` subdirectory, which is where the `build` gate's `cwd`
is set. It is exactly what the gate runs.

- **Release only and x64 only.** Use `dotnet`, never MSBuild.
- **Zero warnings from our code.** The only exempt warnings are the NuGet
  advisories that AGENTS.md lists.

---

## Testing procedure

Tests run on **Microsoft.Testing.Platform** (xUnit v3), from each test
project's own folder, over what the build produced:

```
dotnet test --no-build -c Release
dotnet test --no-build -c Release --filter-method "BerremanTests.SolverTests.*" --filter-method "BerremanTests.SolverTests"
dotnet test --no-build -c Release --filter-trait "Category=ui-smoke"
```

- Filter with xUnit v3's own options only (`--filter-class`,
  `--filter-method`, `--filter-trait`, `--filter-not-trait`). VSTest's
  `--filter` does not exist here.
- `BerremanTests` takes about 52 minutes whole, so run the classes you
  touched. The two constructor suites take under a minute, and
  `ui-tests` about three.
- The ELEV analyzers run over what you changed, from the repo root,
  after the build:

  ```
  powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File Elevation/Run-ElevationGate.ps1 -ExcludeRules ELEV004
  ```

- No test, fixture or kit lives under Documents; test kits and
  databases go under the test run's output directory.
- When a development run exceeds its effective gate deadline, report the gate,
  measured duration and deadline in the state-of-the-world's Tests section.
  The supervisor enforces `attempt_timeout_seconds`, else
  `runtime_estimate_seconds`, from the step's `.gates` snapshot. For spec 0050
  from step 0210, read `specs/0050/.manual/015-ui-smoke-deadline.md` for the
  approved deadline increase and normal profile-1 recovery.

---

## Gates

(Data version 7.) The arc-runner reads each step's gate roster from
the per-step snapshot `specs/<NNN>/.slices/<step>.gates`, which the
step-compiler regenerates at boot from the spec's frozen
`.spec-gates`. The descriptors live under `.gates/`:

- `build` -- `dotnet build` of the solution;
- `unit-tests` -- `BerremanTests`;
- `constructor-unit-tests` -- `OpticalConstructor.Tests`;
- `ui-smoke` and `ui-tests` -- `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, split by
  the `Category=ui-smoke` trait;
- `elevation` and `elevation-full` -- the ELEV analyzers over the
  projects a step touches (plus their dependents), and over every
  project.

The step's `.gates` snapshot is the truth for the step; do not
duplicate it here. What you need to know while implementing:

- **Every step runs every gate in its roster**, in the order
  declared. The first failure short-circuits.
- **`count_at_least` gates** (the test gates) pass when the captured
  count is at least the baseline from the prior green step's
  checkpoint record (`.checkpoints-json`, maintained by the
  arc-runner). You never author baselines yourself.
- **The tree is ELEV-clean.** The known-findings list
  (`Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json`) is empty, so every ELEV
  finding (ELEV004 excepted) fails `elevation`:
  - every line you write is ELEV-clean;
  - never add an entry to the list, and never edit
    `.elevation-analyzers.json` or the analyzers to silence a finding;
  - a mark (`[<ElevationBoundary>]`, `[<NumericCarrier>]`) goes on a
    declaration, never on a module, and only where AGENTS.md allows it.

---

## Code style

**Canonical source:** `./AGENTS.md`, with `./naming_conventions.md` for
names. The rules every edit is held to include:

- elevate every primitive;
- unique names;
- interpolated strings;
- `name : Type`;
- explicit public signatures;
- short comments that cite the spec;
- no new comments in project files.

Gates run post-hoc, so a style breach may pass a gate, but the operator
reads every commit at arc end.

For floating-point comparisons in tests, reuse the tolerance helpers in
`BerremanTests/MatrixComparison.fs`.

---

Per the layout in `arc-runner.system-md`, the per-arc artifacts
folder is `<specs_root>/<spec_id>/.artifacts/` (the supervisor
resolves the concrete absolute path and passes it to the worker
via the task file). Worker code MUST route persistent output to
sub-paths of that folder; never to `%TEMP%/...` or
`%LOCALAPPDATA%/...`.

---

## Commit attribution

**Drop the hard-coded
`Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>`
line**. Replace with `Co-Authored-By: <model> <noreply@<provider>>`
derived from the resolved backend.

---

## Critics

Per-project critic hook. The arc-runner reads the fenced YAML
below at boot, validates each `id` against
`src/schemas/multistep/`, and slots each project critic into the
critic + judge sub-loop after its `run_after` dependencies.
Berreman declares no project critics yet -- the built-in
`architecture_critic` and `reuse_critic` cover the common cases
for this project's numerical / analytics shape.

```yaml
critics: []
```

No project may add a second judge (the `code_judge` is the single
decision point per cycle); the supervisor refuses to start when an
entry's `id` is reserved.

