## Standing operator rulings (every spec)

At spec 0050 steps 0252, 0254, 0259, 0260 and 0261, every role also reads
`specs/0050/.manual/016-step-0252-recommit-fixture.md`. Preserve the copied-item
fixture's three stored items through later slot changes and reuse the shared
ordered Result collector. The 0252 recovery resumes normally with profile 1,
without `--accept-current-slice`, to record measured checkpoint 251.

These bind every role on every step of every spec, a post-mortem's
proposals included. A project prompt states its own rulings because
ASG cannot; these are the ones STL's prompt carries (ASG spec 0090
`.manual/014` section 6), plus the operator's ruling on deferral.

1. **Nothing is deferred** (operator, 2026-11-01; STL spec 0229
   `.manual/006`). A step finishes what its brief asks for. Work that
   cannot be finished is a blocked step naming the question. It is never a "later", never a follow-up, and never an
   entry left for another step.
2. **A published spec is not amended.** An operator ruling in the
   spec's `.manual/`, or an operator note, is the amendment.
3. **Committed green work resumes with `--accept-current-slice`**, not
   with a relaunch that re-runs the worker.
4. **No failure allowance, waiver or carried red.**

For spec 0050, every role reads
`specs/0050/.manual/005-step-0056-parity-retirement.md` at steps 0056, 0057,
0210 and 0354. It authorizes early parity retirement while preserving step
0057's test effects, normal verification and measured-count checkpoint.

At steps 0059, 0151, 0152 and 0260, every role also reads
`specs/0050/.manual/006-step-0059-case-count-accounting.md`. It corrects
method-versus-case retirement arithmetic without changing test effects or
gates. Its explicit 0059 recovery exception requires a normal profile-1 resume
to record the measured checkpoint, without `--accept-current-slice`.

At step 0132, every role also reads
`specs/0050/.manual/009-step-0132-lock-guard-recovery.md`. It authorizes the
shared storage-guard repair and existing-test extensions outside the original
attachment slice's effects. Its explicit recovery exception requires a normal
profile-1 resume after the operator's commit to record checkpoint 131, without
`--accept-current-slice`. Later edits to the shared guard preserve that repaired
contract, including steps 0133, 0138, 0196, 0204, 0307 and 0484.

For spec 0050, every role also reads
`specs/0050/.manual/010-step-0145-scratch-kit-construction.md` at 0145 and when
creating or consuming scratch-kit and scene initializers (especially 0150,
0152–0154 and the forward inventory in that ruling). It authorizes the
Storage-owned, Result-returning constructor and required downstream signature
changes, preserving canonical serialization and typed errors. Its 0145 recovery
exception requires normal profile-1 resume after the operator's commit to record
checkpoint 144, without `--accept-current-slice`.

At step 0150, every role also reads
`specs/0050/.manual/011-step-0150-warning-and-picker-recovery.md`. It authorizes
the inherited JSON-index warning repair and direct kit-picker coverage inside
the existing UI facts. An incremental zero-warning summary does not clear a
previous diagnostic without source repair and recompilation. Its recovery
exception requires normal profile-1 resume after the operator's commit to record
checkpoint 149, without `--accept-current-slice`. Later edits preserve the
corrected indexing and extended picker assertions.

At steps 0160 and 0354, every role also reads
`specs/0050/.manual/012-step-0160-material-schema-recovery.md`. Material metadata
schemas validate structure; category membership is resolved through the caller's
list. Extract the effective schema without the obsolete JSON category enum and
preserve all accepted export/import assertions. Its explicit 0160 recovery
exception requires normal profile-1 resume after the operator's commit to record
checkpoint 159 and measured case evidence, without `--accept-current-slice`.

For spec 0050 from step 0160 onward, also read
`specs/0050/.manual/013-arc-origin-elevation-recovery.md`. Elevation covers all
committed and uncommitted arc changes from the immutable `.arc-base-json`
origin supplied by ASG. Operator commits never narrow that scope. Preserve the
0160 normal-resume exception and its measured checkpoint requirement.

At steps 0185, 0187, 0188 and 0260, every role also reads
`specs/0050/.manual/014-step-0185-read-only-scene-fixture.md`. It authorizes the
scene-save fixture repair and the launcher acceptance test's disabled-Save
expectations, preserving separate UI, model-guard and storage-refusal coverage.
Its 0185 recovery exception
requires normal resume with `--executability-profile 1` after the operator's
commit, without `--accept-current-slice`, to record measured checkpoint 184
before 0186. Preserve the repaired fixture through the later setup-test rename.

The repository's own walls, from AGENTS.md:

- **Never bump a version ring**, Berreman's or STL's.
- **STL (`C:\GitHub\Softellect`) and ASG are read-only from here.**
  Never build them or edit them.
- **Never touch `*.nb` files.**
- **LF line endings.**

---

## Don't ask the user

The arc-runner is the reviewer. The user is NOT watching the
worker session. If the slice spec is ambiguous, pick the
interpretation most consistent with `arc-runner.system-md`, with
this file, and with the surrounding code -- and record the
choice you made in the impl-log's `Gotchas` section.

Prompts that wait for user input will stall the whole round and
escalate after the retry is also stalled. The arc-runner's
workaround is "kill the stalled console and try again once" --
not a replacement for picking a sensible default and noting it.

---

## Operator note

This section is reserved as a stable insertion point for the
arc-runner supervisor. The supervisor injects the operator's
reply text from the previous escalation here on the first
attempt of a resumed slice. When no operator reply is in flight
this heading remains present but empty. Workers MUST read
whatever lands under this heading before acting on the slice
spec; an operator note may add scope constraints or override the
spec for that attempt.
